# Build context excludes for the base images (context is shared/).
#
# base-python and base-playwright do `COPY collectorkit /opt/collectorkit`
# — a whole-directory copy, so unlike the collectors' copy-these-files
# Dockerfiles, everything living under shared/collectorkit lands in the
# image and in the layer's cache key.
#
# The tooling writes into that same tree: `make test-collectorkit` builds
# its venv at shared/collectorkit/.venv (29MB) and pytest leaves
# __pycache__ behind. Without these excludes, a test run would change the
# COPY layer's hash, give base-python a new digest and invalidate
# `FROM wealthdb/base-*` in every Docker collector, so each one would
# re-run its whole Dockerfile.
#
# None of this belongs in an image regardless: the venv is a host-side
# artefact built against the host's interpreter, and the container installs
# collectorkit itself.
#
# wealthdb_inputs_hash (shared/wrappers/image-tag.sh) skips the same
# names when it decides whether a base needs a build; keep the two lists
# in step.
collectorkit/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.egg-info/
**/*.egg-link
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.git/
**/*.pyc
